From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Desidero <desidero@gmail.com>
Date: Tue, 29 Sep 2026 14:35:50 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] feat(web): pick the account a new session runs on

Carried on custom while the design is discussed on upstream issue #503;
see docs/providers.md. Drop it once upstream has an equivalent.

With several providers for one harness on a host, e.g. two Claude Max
accounts and a Databricks workspace, the new-session composer had no way
to choose between them.

An Account section in the harness menu, next to Model and Effort, lists the
host's providers for the selected harness and sends the pick as
provider_override. It stays hidden unless there is more than one choice,
defaults to the host's default provider, drops a pick that no longer applies
after switching host or harness family, and shows accounts that are not
signed in as disabled. It lives in the menu rather than the composer toolbar
so the toolbar keeps room for Send on phones.

Project settings gain an Account field, stored as `provider` in the
project's client-owned config. New sessions in the project start on that
account and the user can still pick another. Where the host can't run the
harness on it, or it isn't signed in, the session uses the host default
and the composer shows why instead of switching accounts silently.

Signed-off-by: Desidero <desidero@gmail.com>
Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
Docs: none (documented with its series in docs/providers.md)
